{
  "version": 3,
  "updated": "2026-08-31",
  "_comment": "Versioned discovery-source catalog. Local only \u2014 unlike the upstream project this was modelled on, nothing here is shared with a community registry and no source metadata leaves the machine. `kind`, `regions`, `roleFamilies` and `requiresSession` drive `apply-agent sources list`. `labels` join a source to the discoverySource strings written into the ledger, which is what makes `apply-agent sources stats` able to report conversion per source. `applicationChannel` is always resolved per job and never assumed from the source.",
  "_measurement": "2026-08-31 (re-measured after widening the feed runner from 2 boards to 7). Public remote aggregators (RemoteOK, We Work Remotely, NoDesk, Working Nomads, Himalayas, Remotive, Jobicy) returned 526 live leads, 221 matching a broad engineering regex, 99 unique companies. Of those, 94 produced slug candidates not already in the pool and ZERO validated as a real Greenhouse/Ashby/Lever/Workable board. ATS links extractable from their descriptions across all seven feeds: 0 \u2014 every board rewrites the apply link to its own detail page. Against a 24.7k-token pool these feeds are catalogued for completeness and cost ~35s to sweep, but they are not a volume source. The upstream community job registry is the opposite: 306 rows of real employer URLs produced 25 new verified board tokens and 44 queue-ready verified-live matches, because its rows come from confirmed applications rather than from a board that monetises the click.",
